# RULE: UX/UI For Electron React Softphone

This is a mandatory Cursor rule.

UX/UI requirements are defined in:

```txt
docs/softphone/UX-UI-Design-Blueprint.md
docs/softphone/UI-Architecture.md
docs/softphone/UI-Design-System.md
docs/softphone/UI-Component-Catalog.md
```

Read `UI-Architecture.md` before any renderer change (hooks, shells, components, stores).

## UX Before UI

Before implementing a user-visible component define:

- affected `LF-XXX` IDs
- visual states
- loading states
- error states
- disabled states
- recovery states
- accessibility behavior
- test IDs

Do not create React components before state design is clear.

## Component Boundary

React components may:

- render props
- emit callbacks
- compose UI-only hooks
- show projections

React components must not:

- call SIP
- call Electron
- call WebSocket
- call repositories
- own business rules
- parse integration payloads

## Electron UX

Electron shell behavior belongs outside React business logic.

Main process may own:

- tray
- window lifecycle
- native notifications
- app close behavior
- minimize and restore

Renderer may display:

- shell projections
- warnings
- user controls

## Required Global States

The UI must represent:

- booting
- OCP authenticating
- OCP session exists
- OCP invalid token
- SIP registering
- SIP registered
- SIP registration failed
- DND
- OCP disconnected
- incoming ringing
- active call
- held call
- transfer mode
- failed operation
- collapsed mode

## Disabled Controls

Every disabled critical control must have a reason.

Examples:

- not registered
- OCP reserved
- invalid number
- second session disabled
- DND active
- transfer in progress
- reconnecting

Disabled state must come from projection, not local component guesses.

## Accessibility

Every interactive control must have:

- keyboard access
- visible focus
- accessible label
- non-color-only state indicator

Critical actions require clear labels:

- answer
- reject
- hang up
- hold
- resume
- mute
- transfer
- retry

## CSS Modules And Tokens (UI-4)

Mandatory for renderer UI work after 2026-06-25 foundation:

- Read `docs/softphone/P11-CSS-Modules-Tokens-Migration.md` before styling changes.
- New or touched `components/**`, `shells/**`, `widgets/**` → co-located `*.module.css` + `var(--*)` from `src/renderer/styles/tokens.css`.
- Do **not** add new global classes to `styles.css`; remove migrated blocks when moving a component to modules.
- Use `clsx` for conditional/variant classes.

## Completion Check

Before finishing UI work verify:

- UX state inventory exists
- component remains presentational
- Use Cases are called outside component internals
- accessibility is covered
- critical call state is visible
- Electron behavior is not mixed with Domain logic
